<title>LEBANON: PAN ARAB GAMES-IRAQ AND KUWAIT TO COMPETE IN PAN ARAB GAMES.</title>
<headline>PAN ARAB GAMES-IRAQ AND KUWAIT TO COMPETE IN PAN ARAB GAMES.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty countries, including Iraq and Kuwait, have confirmed their participation in the Pan Arab Games in Beirut from July 12-27, the organising committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Kuwaiti government had earlier told the committee it might boycott the games if Iraq participated.</p>
<p>The games will be held at a new 50,000-capacity stadium in Beirut and eight suburban locations around the Lebanese capital.</p>
